quickjs-ng v0.17.0: JS_ToCStringLen2 leaks the string reference taken by js_force_tostring when
the UTF-8 buffer allocation fails (out of memory). In the sandbox a script could repeat that near
the heap limit and keep the leaked bytes counted against its own heap. Found by LeakSanitizer
(core_test, result conversion near the heap limit).

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index 6ca030b..d9b44ba 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -4950,6 +4950,7 @@ const char *JS_ToCStringLen2(JSContext *ctx, size_t *plen, JSValueConst val1,
         *plen = str_new->len;
     return (const char *)str8(str_new);
 fail:
+    JS_FreeValue(ctx, val); /* JS_EXCEPTION when js_force_tostring failed: a no-op */
     if (plen)
         *plen = 0;
     return NULL;
